      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-05T09:45:15Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-05T09:51:55Z",
      "duration_ms": 400000,
      "summary": [
        "Implemented the Strategy GUI frontend (WP-008): created views/strategy.js with renderStrategyList and renderStrategyDetail view functions, added five repository CRUD API client methods to api-client.js (listRepos, getRepo, createRepo, updateRepo, deleteRepo), wired two SPA routes (#/strategy and #/strategy/:repoId) into router.js, added the Strategy nav link and script tag to index.html. Updated router-utils.test.ts to stub the two new render functions and added three new router dispatch tests for the strategy routes. All 3058 tests pass."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/public/api-client.js",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/views/strategy.js",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/router.js",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/index.html",
          "mcp-server/tests/gui/router-utils.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T09:51:55Z",
          "note": "views/strategy.js: The vision status badge logic (visionStatus function) checks has_any vs has_full using field truthiness. If the backend returns an empty-string vision field (not null), this correctly detects it as no-vision. The logic is sound but slightly verbose — could be extracted to a shared utility if a second view ever needs vision status display."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T09:51:55Z",
          "note": "api-client.js: The repo CRUD methods follow the established single-line style for simple endpoints (listRepos, getRepo, createRepo, updateRepo, deleteRepo). Consistent with the pattern used by getConfig, getInsights, etc."
