        {
          "type": "bug",
          "priority": "high",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T09:55:52Z",
          "note": "views/strategy.js renderStrategyList — visionStatus(repo) uses 'repo.vision' (expecting the full { short_term, mid_term, long_term } object), but API.listRepos() returns RepoListItem which only carries 'has_vision: boolean' (no 'vision' property). When visionStatus() checks '!vision', vision is undefined, so the function always returns the 'No vision (badge-blocked)' path. Repos with partial or full vision will incorrectly display 'No vision'. Fix: use repo.has_vision boolean directly in visionStatus(), e.g. if (!repo.has_vision) return badge-blocked; and distinguish partial vs full requires either (a) returning the vision object from the list API, or (b) adding has_full_vision: boolean to the list API response alongside has_vision."
        },
        {
          "type": "edge-case",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T09:55:52Z",
          "note": "The Strategy nav link (href='#/strategy') is not highlighted when navigating to a detail page (#/strategy/:repoId). The updateNavActive() function does an exact path match — '/strategy/my-repo' != '/strategy'. This is consistent with existing SPA behavior: the Projects link also doesn't highlight on #/projects/:repo/:slug routes. Not a bug for this WP, but worth noting as a UX consideration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-05T09:56:59Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-05T09:58:16Z",
